# Track the reproducible Splatter scaling workflow while continuing to ignore
# unrelated local scripts and all generated benchmark outputs.
!scripts/
scripts/*
!scripts/benchmark_logging.py
!scripts/generate_splatter_population_benchmark.R
!scripts/run_splatter_population_uot_benchmark.py
!scripts/run_splatter_gene_perturbation_benchmark.py
!scripts/run_splatter_dual_backbone_calibrated_case.py
!scripts/run_splatter_partial_ot_comparator_case.py
!scripts/build_n1000_combined_mass_deficit_f1_report.py
!scripts/aggregate_confidenceot_grid.py
!scripts/finalize_splatter_scaling_benchmark.py
!scripts/make_journal_figure.py
!scripts/make_figure2.py
!scripts/make_method_schematic.py
!scripts/tacc/
scripts/tacc/*
!scripts/tacc/generate_splatter_scaling.slurm
!scripts/tacc/run_splatter_scaling_array.slurm
!scripts/tacc/finalize_splatter_scaling.slurm
!scripts/tacc/submit_splatter_scaling.sh
!scripts/tacc/install_splatter_dependencies.slurm
!scripts/tacc/r_environment.sh
!scripts/tacc/prepare_r_sctransform.slurm
*.inspect.ndjson
*.zip

# Keep one GitHub-facing README; ignore manuscript and internal Markdown notes
*.md
*.MD
!/README.md
!/CURRENT_WORK_SUMMARY_2026-09-13.md
# A prespecification is only worth what its commit timestamp says, so it is
# tracked rather than folded into the summary after the fact.
!/cancer_metastasis/DEG_PRESPECIFICATION_2026-09-15.md
# The deck is generated, so review feedback has to live where the generator
# does or the next rebuild silently drops it.
!/cancer_metastasis/REPORT_DECK_FEEDBACK.md
# The screen's design, written before its results, for the same reason the
# prespecification is tracked.
!/cancer_metastasis/DEPTH_SCREEN_SETUP.md
# The standing answer on the depth confound, and the caveats that come with
# it. Tracked because the splatter round overturned what the screen's own
# outcome section concluded, and that reversal must not live only in a chat.
!/cancer_metastasis/SEQUENCING_DEPTH_RESOLUTION.md

# What was run on 2026-09-23 and how it is to be read, fixed before any of
# it returned. The point of the file is that it predates the numbers, which
# is only checkable if its commit does too.
!/cancer_metastasis/EXPERIMENT_2026-09-23_PREPROCESSING_ARMS.md

# The scoring, tracked apart from the figures that state the setting. A
# metric agreed in a chat and then read off a plot is a metric that can be
# chosen after seeing the numbers.
!/BENCHMARK_METRICS.md

# What lives in the schematic folder and the command that rebuilds each one.
# The images themselves stay untracked; the scripts are what is tracked.
!/figures/schematic/README.md

